Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:33:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] lakeside water-ref candidate 1/2: fix the v_color double
 decode in lakeside-water.effect + refit the water to the r5h3 GRADED sample
 points

CANDIDATE, not for r3 unless Grok Bot approves.
Verified: glTF COLOR_0 is linear by spec and in LK_lake.glb (shallow #7FE0CF stored 0.212/0.745/0.624, deep 0.012/0.275/0.365,
UNSIGNED_BYTE normalized); Cocos 3.8.8 maps COLOR_0 to a_color unchanged (docs: attribute rename only; the Mac-calibrated
emulator reproduces Mac v3.2 near water 64/218/216 only with exactly one x^2 on it, i.e. the shader's). Line 89
SRGBToLinear(v_color) therefore decoded it a second time (R 0.212 -> 0.045). Now albedo *= v_color.rgb.
(builtin-standard does the same SRGBToLinear on vertex colours - Cocos convention; for the palette meshes those are grey AO,
left untouched here.)
Refit (Grok Bot: targets stay the r5h3 GRADED values, sample.py boxes on the graded 8 s time median; global lights/fog untouched):
waterTint 0.9/1/1 -> 0.507/0.981/1.0 (graded saturation), main 1.37 -> 1.28, ambient 1.85 -> 2.0, sky strength 0.35 -> 0
(night 0.12 -> 0), floor 0.31 -> 0.39 (params + effect defaults). Water fallback mainColor follows (129/250/255).
Stand-in (emulator): near_water_bottom 56/152/145 -> 67/147/137 (target 55/148/147, both pass), near_water_L 59/153/146 ->
70/148/138 (67/151/146, pass); mid 161/141/128 -> 137/133/130 (77/120/125, fail, fog-lifted); mid_R 160/146/133 ->
138/140/135; far 183/153/129 -> 155/135/129 (92/88/80, fail, fog); near-mid / under-bridge still fail (~R +45); stripe 5.0 -> 4.0.
Tests water_fog / daynight follow.
